@@ -3,3 +3,14 @@
 A small TypeScript library, with no runtime dependency, of building blocks for our services that store,
 exchange and update JSON: configuration files, API payloads and stored records. It is imported by the
 other projects of the team, so its behaviour must follow the published standards it implements.
+
+## JSON Pointer (RFC 6901)
+
+`resolvePointer(document, pointer)`, exported from `src/index.ts`, returns the value of `document` that
+`pointer` refers to. The empty pointer returns the whole document. It throws an `Error` when the pointer
+is not a valid JSON Pointer (it must be empty or start with `/`, and `~` must be followed by `0` or `1`),
+or when it does not resolve: missing member, array index out of range or not canonical (no leading
+zeros), the `-` token (it names no existing element), or a step into a primitive. Only own members of
+objects are resolved, so `/__proto__` or `/length` never reach inherited properties.
+
+Run the tests with `npm test`.
diff --git a/src/index.ts b/src/index.ts
